CONTEXT
    Preparation and publication require an attached HEAD, a fully clean index and
    tree including untracked files and submodules, and no merge, rebase, cherry-pick,
    or revert. Resolve operation markers through Git for worktrees. The task branch
    must pass Git branch-ref validation, contain the exact active ticket token, and
    differ from the explicitly selected destination branch. Follow current project
    AGENTS.md and explicit user naming overrides, not old conversation conventions.
    Without an override use <type>/<TICKET-ID>-<lowercase-kebab-description>, with
    feature/bugfix/hotfix/chore/refactor/perf/test/release and 1–6 description words.

    Resolve the correct push and destination remotes. Fetch only the explicitly
    selected target from its destination remote, record its exact ref and revision,
    and find its merge base with HEAD. No fallback target or unrelated base is allowed;
    missing shared ancestry fails. The target_ref..HEAD range must be nonempty. Check
    every SHA and full commit message, including merges. Preserve message whitespace
    except record separators and one terminal newline. Follow project commit rules;
    otherwise require one <TICKET-ID>: <Capitalized present-tense summary> line with
    the exact ticket once and no body or extra prefix. Use no generated validator.

    Review the complete merge-base-to-HEAD diff and verify messages and draft claims
    against implementation. Follow exact imports or symbols only for material gaps.
    Run only missing project-required checks for unchanged code and inputs, preserving
    all exits and never masking failures. Inspect a targeted manifest/Makefile only
    when needed; probe runtime health only after an actual failure. All required
    checks must pass, material correctness concerns must be resolved, and ticket work
    must be complete. Recheck branch, HEAD, target revision, task, Git operation state,
    full index/tree, and saved draft immediately before saving or publication.
AS git_rules
